Package: pnsbib
Type: Package
Title: Probabilities of Causation with Partial Information
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Marek", "Deja", email = "marek.deja@uj.edu.pl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes Li and Pearl's (2024) <doi:10.1609/aaai.v38i18.30030>
    multivalued probabilities-of-causation
    bounds from observational and interventional distributions, with exact
    finite response-type linear-programming bounds for tractable problems.
    Supports complete-margin, partial-information and longitudinal finite
    categorical models, sensitivity analysis, sampling-region projection
    and graphics. Data acquisition, outcome construction and causal
    identification are separate from the bounds engine. Bibliometric coverage
    is one application of the general probability-table interface.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: lpSolve, graphics, grDevices, digest
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), rzig (>= 0.2.3), knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/build/clean-inst-doc: FALSE
SystemRequirements: Zig 0.16.0 (obtained automatically in temporary storage
    during source installation if unavailable)
URL: https://github.com/MarekDejaUJ/pnsbib
